  \frac{q_i^+}{q_i^-}\leq s_+\{1+O(\delta)+O(C^{-1})\}\leq\vartheta<1
 \]
 after decreasing $\delta$, where $s_+=1/r_-$.  They also give
 $q_i^--q_i^+\geq\kappa_0i$ in the displayed clock.  The product-odds formula
 for the dominated nearest-neighbor walk proves \eqref{eq:green-macro}.
