  1182	\section{Pair gates and the complete post-establishment path}
  1183	
  1184	For the center, let
  1185	\[
  1186	 I_H=\sum_{x\ {\rm in\ clique}}\frac1{d_x}
  1187	 =1+\frac1{C-1+m},
  1188	\qquad
  1189	 J_H(r)=\sum_{x\ {\rm in\ clique}}
  1190	 \frac{h_H^{\dB}(\{x\};r)}{d_x},
  1191	\]
  1192	where $h_H^{\dB}$ is the isolated-center dB fixation committor.
  1193	For a pair with internal weight $W=C/\sigma$, put
  1194	\[
  1195	 I_P=\frac2W=\frac{2\sigma}{C},\qquad
  1196	 J_P(r)=\frac1W=\frac{\sigma}{C}.
  1197	\]
  1198	The second identity uses the exact dB singleton value $1/2$ on $K_2$.
  1199	The center estimates imply
  1200	\[
  1201	 I_H=1+o(1),\qquad J_H(r)=p+o(1),
  1202	\]
  1203	while $J_H(1/r)$ and the reciprocal core fixation probability are
  1204	$o(C^{-1})$.
  1205	
  1206	\begin{proposition}[Gate odds and global sweep]
  1207	\label{prop:gate}
  1208	For every fixed $r>1$, the separated macro-fixation probabilities satisfy
  1209	\[
  1210	 P_U^H=1-o(q/C),
  1211	 \qquad
  1212	 P_{\Bd}^P\longrightarrow\frac{Z_B}{1+Z_B},
  1213	 \qquad
  1214	 P_{\dB}^P\longrightarrow\frac{Z_D}{1+Z_D},
  1215	\]
  1216	where
  1217	\[
  1218	 Z_B=\sigma(r^2-1),\qquad
  1219	 Z_D=\frac{2r(r-1)}{\sigma}.
  1220	\]
  1221	The convergence is uniform when $r$ ranges over a compact subinterval of
  1222	$(1,\infty)$.
  1223	\end{proposition}
  1224	
  1225	\begin{proof}
  1226	For one specified pair, let $A,D,B,C'$ denote, respectively, mutant-pair
  1227	invasion of a resident center, resident-center recovery of that pair,
  1228	mutant-center invasion of a resident pair, and resident-pair recovery of
  1229	the center.  In each row below $a_P$ means the isolated pair fixation
  1230	$a_P^U$ for that update rule.  Summing the parent--target or death--parent events gives,
  1231	after a common time change,
  1232	\[
  1233	\begin{array}{c|cccc}
  1234	 &A&D&B&C'\\ \hline
  1235	 \Bd&
  1236	 CrI_Pu_{\rm core}^{\Bd}(r)&
  1237	 2I_Ha_P(1/r)&
  1238	 2rI_Ha_P(r)&
  1239	 CI_Pu_{\rm core}^{\Bd}(1/r)\\[1mm]
  1240	 \dB&
  1241	 2rJ_H(r)&
  1242	 (C/r)J_P(1/r)&
  1243	 CrJ_P(r)&
  1244	 (2/r)J_H(1/r).
  1245	\end{array}
  1246	\]
  1247	The isolated pair values are
  1248	\[
  1249	 a_P^{\Bd}(r)=\frac r{r+1},\quad
  1250	 a_P^{\Bd}(1/r)=\frac1{r+1},\quad
  1251	 a_P^{\dB}(r)=a_P^{\dB}(1/r)=\frac12.
  1252	\]
  1253	
  1254	On macro states the only nonzero rates are
  1255	\[
  1256	\begin{array}{ll}
  1257	 (0,k)\to(1,k):kA,&(0,k)\to(0,k-1):kD,\\
  1258	 (1,k)\to(1,k+1):(q-k)B,&(1,k)\to(0,k):(q-k)C'.
  1259	\end{array}
  1260	\]
  1261	From $(1,k)$, the chance that the center reverses before the next pair
  1262	conversion is $C'/(B+C')$.  A union bound over at most $q$ conversions gives
  1263	\[
  1264	 1-P_U^H\le q\frac{C'}{B+C'}.
  1265	\]
  1266	Proposition~\ref{prop:center} and the portal estimates give
  1267	$qC'/B=o(q/C)$, uniformly on each fitness compact.  Thus a mutant center
  1268	converts all resident pairs with probability $1-o(q/C)$.
  1269	
  1270	From $(0,1)$, the first successful macro event is either center invasion at
