   951	After a seed, stop the ordinary count on $\{0,K\}$.  For every hidden hub
   952	and pendant state, the Bd up/down odds on $1\leq i<K$ are at least a fixed
   953	$r_1>1$.  The conditional-bias argument therefore gives
   954	$\Prob_1(\tau_K<\tau_0)\geq p_0>0$.  The embedded walk makes $O(K)$ expected
   955	changes, and its changing intensity is bounded below, so
   956	$\mathbb E\tau_{0,K}=O(K)$.  The distinguished-pendant loss intensity is at
   957	most $1/d$, giving $O(K/C)$ loss during this stopped trial.  If the count
   958	hits zero while the pendant survives, wait for resident-hub regeneration,
   959	suppressing or deleting every ordinary reseed and every additional mutant
   960	pendant until hub loss.  This is again an adverse graphical coupling: the
   961	distinguished pendant cannot be lost while its sole neighbor is mutant, and
   962	any subsequent resident-phase loss is charged as trial failure.  Delete the
   963	extra mutants again at regeneration.  If it hits $K$, the preceding completion
