     1	# Paper II superseding-version release notes
     2	
     3	## Result
     4	
     5	Let `R_hyb` be the unique root in `(3/2,151/100)` of
     6	
     7	\[
     8	R^6-8R^5+22R^4-30R^3+21R^2-6R+1.
     9	\]
    10	
    11	One fitness-independent family of finite connected loopless undirected
    12	weighted graphs simultaneously amplifies every fixed `1<r<R_hyb` for all
    13	sufficiently large population indices.  Thus
    14	
    15	\[
    16	R_{\rm sim}\ge R_{\rm hyb}=1.5028569127905696\ldots>3/2.
    17	\]
    18	
    19	The release also gives a specialization with entirely rational edge weights
    20	and threshold `1.50176815223369...>3/2`.  It proves optimality among fixed
    21	positive parameters in the displayed first-order pair--pendant response
    22	model.  It does not determine the unrestricted value of `R_sim` or prove a
    23	universal upper bound.
    24	
    25	## Reproducibility boundary
    26	
    27	The standalone 23-member archive contains the manuscript source and PDF,
    28	three paper-local exact certifiers, the paper-level integration audit, pinned
    29	dependencies with their two hash-pinned pure-Python wheels, a verifier
    30	failure-regression test, and deterministic replay/build/release scripts.  The
    31	manuscript itself is the analytic proof.  The archive omits duplicate or stale
    32	proof notes, discovery scripts, sparse numerical diagnostics, the retired
    33	affine workstream, temporary compiler products, rendered QA images, virtual
    34	environments, venue metadata, and cover letters.
    35	
    36	The exact programs audit finite transition aggregation and symbolic/rational
    37	identities.  The all-order weak-cut, establishment, cleanup, reciprocal-
    38	invasion, and sweep estimates are analytic arguments in the manuscript and
    39	are not replaced by computation.
    40	
    41	This checkpoint makes two previously compressed stochastic steps explicit:
    42	the Bd cleanup proof now includes a stopped strong-Markov block recursion,
    43	and the reciprocal dB proof includes a finite-horizon exponential-moment
    44	bound for its dominating immigration--death process.
    45	
    46	The final submission correction writes the dB attempt duration as
    47	`T=beta_0(B_0) log C` and displays the two coefficient inequalities that give
    48	the claimed `O(C^(-B_0-2))` coordinate-survival bounds.  The manuscript source
    49	link is frozen at the annotated, unsigned repository tag
    50	`simultaneous-amplification-beyond-three-halves-v2.0.2`.
    51	
    52	The post-referee correction stops pendant synchronization at either its target
    53	state or upper-strip exit.  It gives the exit favorable boundary value in the
    54	trace comparison, proves `O(m)` expected stopped trace outcomes and `O(C)`
    55	calendar time per outcome, and treats the zero-pendant boundary separately.
    56	This fixes two false unstopped expectations without changing the theorem or
    57	any asymptotic scale.
    58	
    59	All verification conditions now raise explicitly and every verifier rejects
    60	optimized Python.  The clean bootstrap exercises disposable exact-identity
    61	and integration-marker mutations and checks that failures propagate without a
    62	whole-replay success sentinel.  Python dependencies install offline from the
    63	bundled hash-pinned wheels; the PDF toolchain remains externally provisioned.
    64	Archive entry-point modes are explicit and checked.  Package hashes establish
    65	internal consistency, not authorship or cryptographic authentication of the
    66	unsigned Git tag.
    67	
    68	## Related public versions
    69	
    70	- <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21852072> is the v1 source/software archive
    71	  containing an earlier manuscript version of the beyond-`3/2` result.
    72	- <https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21850042> is the superseded source/software
    73	  archive for the earlier `R_sim>=3/2` construction.
    74	
    75	Both records are unrefereed repository snapshots rather than peer-reviewed
    76	articles or bioRxiv postings, and neither is the persistent identifier for
    77	this superseding manuscript package.  A new versioned deposit may be named
    78	only after the human author creates it.
